{"kind":"event","event_id":1469,"event_uid":"01M2GR540FEQ0SJD84VS85G1F4","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":23,"project_uid":"01M2GR1P2QP46QS712Q8K0HN49","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers-run-128","issue_id":79,"issue_uid":"01M2GR1QC32PTEP8TNP8XEDWBF","issue_short_id":"dwbf","actor":"impl:1@run-128","hlc_physical_ms":1789416083471,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"8810d1c025464cd4605d080ee095ca78822e3dc9b2ba60a012a3d67313ceee56","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2GR540EJD0SGNVR94A7Z63R","author":"impl:1@run-128","body":"task 1 approach: replace implTestCmdLine/fixTestCmdLine's TEST COMMAND line with a proofsBlock(runs, checks) helper in fleet/run-engine.mjs, built from task.proofRuns and the run's constraintChecks in plan order (Run: lines then Check: lines; the '(none — the driver runs the exam at handoff)' sentence when both are empty). Delete capWorkerParallelism/sharesRunWideCmd/runWideSharers/implTestCmdLine and their explanatory comment paragraphs, plus the incidental capWorkerParallelism mentions at run-engine.mjs:640 and run-main.mjs:77 (the zero-count grep counts comments). Examiner keeps testCmdLine; reconciler keeps its run-wide TEST COMMAND line. Rewrite implementer.md line 7 and rule 2 and the equivalent sentence in fix.md to the PROOFS block. Checked first: neither survivor sim (proof_runs, review_economy) contains the string TEST COMMAND or any of the four symbols, and both print ALL TESTS PASSED at BASE — so the run-127 red was the retired pair/critic legs, not these.","created_at":"2026-09-14T20:01:23.470542134Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-14T20:01:23.471Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":1470,"event_uid":"01M2GR5KDQ74FJCXMERPZZSNXG","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":23,"project_uid":"01M2GR1P2QP46QS712Q8K0HN49","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers-run-128","issue_id":80,"issue_uid":"01M2GR1QYT8XDYA40P925K8S4W","issue_short_id":"8s4w","actor":"impl:2@run-128","hlc_physical_ms":1789416099255,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"9ee02cc418a3af2ac7bf5c39694e17ff7ae24475980f4dbb077bf361d95bdd30","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2GR5KDPKEY9PM246B29V7HQ","author":"impl:2@run-128","body":"task 2 (launch bump recompiles): approach — lift the stamped compile in `launch` into a `compileFor(n)` closure plus a `sizeFromCompile` helper; hand `pushPlan` the first N's compile and `recompile`, and have it recompile once per bumped N (after the purge, before the next attempt's hub filing), returning the compile the winning N was filed under. `launch` then reads width/cpu/memory off that returned compile for the `new` verb. The un-bumped path still makes exactly one stamped compile, before `new`. Capacity (`billing plan --json`) stays checked once on the first compile's size before any mutation: the widest wave does not depend on --stamp, so the recompiled size is the checked one.","created_at":"2026-09-14T20:01:39.254440173Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-14T20:01:39.255Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":1471,"event_uid":"01M2GR9QDTXZ457DDEGYNB7ESJ","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":23,"project_uid":"01M2GR1P2QP46QS712Q8K0HN49","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers-run-128","issue_id":79,"issue_uid":"01M2GR1QC32PTEP8TNP8XEDWBF","issue_short_id":"dwbf","actor":"exam:1@run-128","hlc_physical_ms":1789416234426,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"437e0140bfb19a24ca4422a675cdc27231017c1d4ccc69ca8a92f9efb51fb47e","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2GR9QDSE9C2TMGZJD5VF255","author":"exam:1@run-128","body":"examiner (task 1): writing `fleet/tests/test_run_engine_own_proofs.mjs` as a `_engine_helpers.mjs` rig sim, four scenarios:\n\n- S1 — one task with two Proof `Run:` lines (the second red on pass 0, green after the repair round) plus one Global Constraints `Check:`, and a `t1_test.sh` exam red at BASE / green on the patch. That single run records `impl:T1`, `exam:T1` and `fix:T1:0` prompts, which is legs (a) first half [M1], (b) [M2] and (c) [M3] in one place — and it is why leg (b)'s \"the same `PROOFS:` block\" can be asserted as string equality between the impl and fix prompts of the SAME task rather than across two runs.\n- S2 — a task with no `Run:`, a run with no `Check:`, and the task still carrying its own `testCmd`: leg (a) second half. At BASE that prompt carries `TEST COMMAND: bash check.sh`, so the red is sharp.\n- S3 — the implementer writes the rig's `BROKEN` marker, so the folded tree's `bash check.sh` is red once and a `reconcile:wave1:1` worker is dispatched; the stub removes the marker and reports FIXED so the wave still adopts. Leg (e) [M5].\n- S4/S5 — the two greps as a static source read (leg (d) [M4]) and the two survivor sims' presence + `ALL TESTS PASSED` sentinel (leg (f) [M6]).\n\nTwo readings I am recording because a later session would otherwise have to re-derive them:\n\n1. Block order. M1 says 'one line per Proof `Run:` ... and one line per ... `Check:` ... in plan order', and the Produces interface spells the block `\\nPROOFS:\\n- Run: <cmd>\\n- Check: <cmd>`. I read that as all `- Run: ` lines in `task.proofRuns` order first, then all `- Check: ` lines in `constraintChecks` order — not interleaved — and the exam pins the exact substring.\n2. The examiner's prompt. M3's 'unchanged from BASE' is asserted as: exactly one line beginning `TEST COMMAND:`, and it is exactly `TEST COMMAND: <the exam command>`. I deliberately do NOT assert the examiner has no `PROOFS:` block — nothing in the task asks for one, and pinning its absence would grade a choice the Machine clauses never make.","created_at":"2026-09-14T20:03:54.425063409Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-14T20:03:54.426Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":1472,"event_uid":"01M2GRAAPQ3GH71KRGEDT97QY7","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":23,"project_uid":"01M2GR1P2QP46QS712Q8K0HN49","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers-run-128","issue_id":80,"issue_uid":"01M2GR1QYT8XDYA40P925K8S4W","issue_short_id":"8s4w","actor":"exam:2@run-128","hlc_physical_ms":1789416254167,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"2f14e9737c7be6be6d389ac96beb9f8066e1c140587561a1755c57451dd0aeda","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2GRAAPNTZSQGWGGCMADPJ51","author":"exam:2@run-128","body":"Examiner: writing fleet/tests/test_launch_bump.mjs. Approach: the size sim's scaffolding, copied (its own header sets that convention) — a real target repo from _lobby_helpers with a bare origin, a recording exec, and a fake kata hub that stamps each call with the exec-call index so hub/exec ordering is readable. The bump is made real rather than faked: the rule that refuses the first push of ultra/plan-run-1 first pushes base:refs/heads/ultra/plan-run-1 onto the bare origin, so the launcher's own re-read of highestRunOnTarget sees 1 taken and bumps to 2 on its own. The compiler stub answers a stamp-dependent payload: run-1 -> waves 2/10/1 with sheets under tests/exams/run_1/, run-2 -> waves 2/4/1 with sheets under tests/exams/run_2/. Two payloads is how M3's 'the size the new verb carries is computed from the recompiled payload' becomes falsifiable at all — widest 10 is 6/8GB under the 6/8GB caps, widest 4 is 4/6GB, so a launch that sized off the first compile is red. Legs: (a) two stamped compiles run-1 then run-2, the second ordered after the refused push and before the second createProject, the project-2 sheets deep-equal to the run-2 payload's and no run_1 anywhere in them; (b) un-bumped, exactly one stamped compile before the new verb and 6/8GB as at BASE; (c) the new verb's --comment run=2 and its --cpu/--memory 4/6GB.","created_at":"2026-09-14T20:04:14.165302359Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-14T20:04:14.167Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":1473,"event_uid":"01M2GRFB33VHYSJYC9MSNXWR91","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":23,"project_uid":"01M2GR1P2QP46QS712Q8K0HN49","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers-run-128","issue_id":79,"issue_uid":"01M2GR1QC32PTEP8TNP8XEDWBF","issue_short_id":"dwbf","actor":"exam:1@run-128","hlc_physical_ms":1789416418403,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"2cc0d588fa9e620cb639b31079993c3d04e387e2ebe4fd52c579b0fdc9c4a3d9","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2GRFB31BFRA8V8ANQ9BXH92","author":"exam:1@run-128","body":"examiner (task 1): `fleet/tests/test_run_engine_own_proofs.mjs` is written and red at BASE for one reason — the implementation does not exist yet.\n\nRed at BASE, assertion by assertion (soft-assert run, so every leg was reached rather than stopping at the first):\n\n- leg (a) [M1] — `impl:T1` carries `TEST COMMAND: bash check.sh` (the run-wide suite, via `implTestCmdLine`/`namesProofTest`) and no `PROOFS:` block; same for `impl:T2` in the no-`Run:`/no-`Check:` scenario.\n- leg (b) [M2] — `fix:T1:0` carries `TEST COMMAND: bash t1_test.sh` (the exam command, via `fixTestCmdLine`) and no block.\n- leg (d) [M4] — all four engine symbols present, `TEST COMMAND` present in `implementer.md`, and neither role file names `PROOFS:`. Note `fix.md` does NOT contain the string `TEST COMMAND` at BASE, so that half of the grep is already zero — it says the same thing in its own words, and the exam's extra assertion that each role file NAMES `PROOFS:` is what keeps `fix.md` from passing by doing nothing.\n\nGreen at BASE, and meant to be — these are the preservation clauses:\n\n- leg (c) [M3] — the examiner's one `TEST COMMAND:` line already names the exam command.\n- leg (e) [M5] — the reconciler already carries the run-wide line and no block. The scenario is real, not vacuous: the sim's implementer writes the rig's `BROKEN` marker, the folded tree's `bash check.sh` goes red, and the precondition asserts `reconcile:wave1:1` was actually dispatched before reading its prompt (the stub then removes the marker and reports FIXED, so the wave still adopts).\n- leg (f) [M6] — both survivor sims are present with their sentinel.\n\nWhole file runs in about half a second; `test_sims_are_hermetic.mjs` is green with it in the sweep (15 sims, 0 offenders). Nothing returned unsatisfiable.\n\nFor the implementer: the exam reads LINES, not substrings — `testCmdLinesOf` filters lines that BEGIN `TEST COMMAND:`, because `implementer.md` line 7 and `reconcile.md` line 20 mention the phrase in prose at BASE and that is M4's grep to answer, not M1's. And the block's body is read as the lines under a line that is exactly `PROOFS:`, up to the next `KEY:` line or a blank line, so where the block sits among the other input lines is left free.","created_at":"2026-09-14T20:06:58.401961401Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-14T20:06:58.403Z"}
